aims with point estimates near zero and raw 95% intervals excluding clinically meaningful effects in the registered direction once the comparator scale is considered. H6 and H10 are borderline only because their intervals very narrowly reach the approximate 10%-of-comparator threshold, while point estimates are tiny and statistically non-significant; I left them unresolved but deferred rather than accepting or strongly rejecting them. H1 and H3 are interactions with intervals that still include clinically meaningful ranges; H3 in particular is underpowered/uncertain because one cell is only 62 observations despite valid Welch cells, so both are unresolved and deferred. H8 remains active as an unresolved possible signal: raw estimate approximately -0.022, raw CI approximately [-0.053, +0.009], with interval lower bounds extending beyond a plausible 10% threshold for outcome_011. It is not accepted because the interval includes zero and the point estimate is modest. Overall, H7 is the only discovery robust enough to carry forward now. No causal or generalizable biomarker claim is made from this dataset; the evidence supports only a strong association within this sample for feature_065 and outcome_013, pending validation.",
